{"event": "model_response", "time": 1793350834.6575663, "run_id": "6222ed77274a4da8965a40987f57b9f7", "seq": 198, "number": 13, "response": {"id": "dc4c9365-a1e6-4c3e-9629-2c45bbbcd4e5", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1793350831, "model": "deepseek-flash", "choices": [{"index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "继续接收已排队、本该投递的页面批次（24～31 页），不重复读取来源。\n\n```python\nr = recall(['ev-4e747765f5046c8ad8b1','ev-daeb56e673fc61cae0ef','ev-a30e6edea79391cf315d','ev-1e23be7c32e2bf283689','ev-eb42e63472799e638c3f','ev-81117fe71aa5d10b548d','ev-97c7764bd93b97111551','ev-2c646589154451e7b722'])\nprint(r.get('requested_count'), r.get('queued_count'))\n```", "reasoning_content": "We have pages up to 23 delivered (ev through page 23). Need pages 24-52. The read_pdf call was already made for full range and batches advance. I should recall/queue next batch or just call read_pdf again? Progress says pages missing 20-52 but delivery shows 20-23 delivered. The read_pdf result was queued; batches advance after successful actions. Let me call task_status or recall pending evidence ids.\n\nThe pending batch: ev-4e747765f5046c8ad8b1 etc. Let me recall them — but read_pdf tool advances automatically after successful actions. Simplest: call read_pdf again? It might reread. Instruction: \"Do not print all pages or reread just to advance.\" \"On error use the retained batch.\" So I should recall pending evidence ids.\n\nLet me recall the 8 pending ids."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9131, "completion_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 9475, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 186}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4779}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
