g–acting–interacting 三类，三者层层递进并构成良性循环（推理技术支持更强 acting，助理的交互能力支持社会模拟，助理与社会实验的产出可回流做数据增强）。p.4 原文「The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other: the technology that has been developed by the reasoning approaches (category 1) is used for increasingly intelligent acting by assistants.」检索方法：先用 Google Scholar 搜 Agentic LLM，再用 snowballing 扩展被引文献；只收 LLM 方法，排除无 LLM 的多智能体工作。p.5 原文「The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.」\nEvidence ev-0aaa960f62d9cf1689f1 | paper.pdf | page:11 | sha256=b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c\n                                                                                                                             Agentic LLM      •   1:11\n\n\n     Approach                                      Reasoning Technology            Acting/Assistant                      Interacting\n     Iterated Prisoner’s [Fontana et al., 2024]            LLM                   Cooperate/Defect                      Social Dilemma\n     Social Games [Akata et al., 2025]                     LLM                   Cooperate/Defect                  Battle of the Sexes, etc\n     GTBench [Duan et al., 2024]                         CoT/ToT                 Cooperate/Defect               Kuhn poker, liar’s dice, nim\n     GAMA-Bench [Huang et al., 2024a]                      LLM                   Cooperate/Defect                El Farol, Public Goods, etc\n     Theory of Mind [van Duijn et al., 2023]               LLM                     Theory of Mind                           Stories\n     NegotiationArena [Bianchi et al., 2024]               LLM                         Dialogue                          Negotiation\n     Alympics [Mao et al., 2023]                           LLM                  Multi-agent sandbox              Water-allocation challenge\n     MAgIC [Xu et al.